1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,760
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:02,810 --> 00:00:06,021
AI for Young Builders, video 9.

3
00:00:06,071 --> 00:00:10,230
Teaching AI to read: words and feelings.

4
00:00:11,350 --> 00:00:17,656
Companies read thousands of reviews every day to find out how people feel.

5
00:00:17,706 --> 00:00:20,920
That job is called sentiment analysis.

6
00:00:20,970 --> 00:00:22,380
Let us build one.

7
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:27,851
Just like pictures, words must become numbers.

8
00:00:27,901 --> 00:00:31,822
One simple way is to give each word a score.

9
00:00:31,872 --> 00:00:38,680
Delicious might be plus two, cold minus one, awful minus two, and the, zero.

10
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:43,624
To judge a review, add up its word scores.

11
00:00:43,674 --> 00:00:48,369
The samosa was hot and delicious adds up to plus three.

12
00:00:48,419 --> 00:00:51,130
Above zero means a happy review.

13
00:00:52,450 --> 00:00:54,430
But look at not good.

14
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:59,940
Not scores zero and good scores plus one, so the total is

15
00:00:59,990 --> 00:01:01,487
plus one: happy.

16
00:01:01,537 --> 00:01:02,067
Wrong!

17
00:01:02,117 --> 00:01:07,480
Simple word scores ignore word order, so not fools them.

18
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:10,966
Sarcasm is even trickier.

19
00:01:11,016 --> 00:01:17,032
Oh great, cold samosas again sounds happy word by word, but it is not.

20
00:01:17,082 --> 00:01:22,751
Modern AI looks at whole sentences and word order, and learns from

21
00:01:22,801 --> 00:01:27,690
millions of examples, which is why it needs so much data.

22
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:30,490
Let us recap.

23
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:33,687
Words become numbers for an AI.

24
00:01:33,737 --> 00:01:37,501
Adding word scores gives a sentiment.

25
00:01:37,551 --> 00:01:41,832
Not, and sarcasm, fool simple word scores.

26
00:01:41,882 --> 00:01:47,090
Next: How chatbots write: predicting the next word.
